---
import Layout from '../layouts/ResourceLayout.astro';
import CoverageLab from '../components/CoverageLab.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---
<Layout title="Single-sensor coverage lab" section="Lab · Single-sensor model" heading="What counts as sufficient coverage?"
  description="Move a sensor or change its radius. Compare the fraction of a bounded area covered by its circular footprint with a specified threshold.">
  <p>In the intersection model, <a href={base + 'learn/v3/05-learning-through-models-and-prototypes/#arrival-experiment'}>move one arrival in Chapter 5</a> or <a href={base + 'learn/v3/06-engineering-data-from-measurements-to-decisions/#two-cycle-experiment'}>follow both queues into a second cycle in Chapter 6</a>.</p>
  <p><a href={base + 'learn/01-engineering-intent/#exercise'}>Follow the original Chapter 1 experiment</a> to predict a change, record the reference and try a different configuration.</p>
  <div class="coverage-workspace"><CoverageLab /></div>
  <p><a href={base + 'learn/01-engineering-intent/#evidence'}>Interpret your results</a> · <a href={base + 'reference/'}>Inspect the sources and evidence</a></p>
</Layout>
<style>
  .coverage-workspace { --surface: var(--home-bg); --surface-muted: var(--home-panel); --sage-olive: #6d897f; --deep-olive: var(--home-teal); --autumn-orange: var(--home-gold); --dusty-violet: var(--home-gold); }
  .coverage-workspace :global(fieldset) { min-width: 0; }
  .coverage-workspace :global(input) { color: var(--home-text); }
  .coverage-workspace :global([data-sensor]) { fill: var(--home-bg); stroke: var(--home-text); }
</style>
